	abstract = {If qk is the extinction probability of a slightly supercritical branching process with offspring distribution P kr : r = 0, 1, 2,..., then it is shown that if sup ? r r 3 p kr , 2 k &gt; 0, and m k ? 1, then 1 - q k ~ 2( m k -1)s k -2 , where m k = ? r rp kr , s 2 k = ? k r r 2 p kr - m k 2 . This provides a simple set of sufficient conditions for the validity of a conjecture of Ewens (1969) for the survival probability of a slightly advantageous mutant gene.},
